[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define eligibility-checked inventory, party progression, and stable reward
[stderr] +application rules that protect required items and prevent dead ends. This task
[stderr] +owns shared contracts, not authored items, values, presentation, or economy.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0004 provides immutable state and idempotent commands; R0015 provides stable
[stderr] +reward resolution and one-time reward IDs. Their implementation ownership
[stderr] +remains intact. GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for authored item and
[stderr] +progression shapes; it does not defer this contract's authoring.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/core/campaign/{inventory,party}*` and
[stderr] +  `tests/core/campaign/inventory*`.
[stderr] +- Item, eligibility, party-progression, and reward-application envelopes.
[stderr] +- Shared inventory commands and protected-required-item invariants.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Model inventory and party progression using stable identifiers, explicit
[stderr] +eligibility predicates, and immutable transitions. Validate item existence,
[stderr] +ownership, expected revision, target eligibility, prerequisite state, and the
[stderr] +originating reward before mutation. Ineligible use, missing items, duplicate
[stderr] +reward application, and stale commands are no-ops with typed rejection or the
[stderr] +recorded prior outcome. Required items cannot be destructively discarded,
[stderr] +consumed, traded, or overwritten in a way that makes the required abstract
[stderr] +route impossible.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Web and PWA adapters submit the same inventory/progression commands and render
[stderr] +the returned state/events. Inventory controls, drag/drop, responsive layout,
[stderr] +notifications, persistence-driver choices, and installed-PWA lifecycle are
[stderr] +outside this contract.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not author items, party members, progression values, inventory UI, crafting,
[stderr] +trading, purchases, destructive discard, art, audio, maps, remote state, or
[stderr] +browser/PWA behavior. Do not resolve GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: abstract inventory and party rules need no
[stderr] +visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve item icons, portraits, sprites,
[stderr] +textures, fonts, illustrations, maps, or other product assets; `asset_ids`
[stderr] +remains blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract owns no music or sound-effect
[stderr] +trigger, selection, or mix. Keep audio IDs, brief, and style version blank and
[stderr] +do not create incidental cues.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Use deterministic fixtures to prove eligibility is checked before mutation
[stderr] +  and that missing/ineligible/stale commands preserve the exact prior state.
[stderr] +- Prove duplicate reward IDs do not apply twice and protected required items
[stderr] +  cannot be lost in a way that removes the required abstract route.
[stderr] +- Compare metadata, requirements, dependencies, ownership, and provenance with
[stderr] +  IMP-0016 and R0016's manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain inventory/progression rejection fixtures, duplicate-reward and
[stderr] +protected-item invariant results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and the
[stderr] +unresolved GATE-0004 record.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Eligibility is validated before inventory or party-progression mutation.
[stderr] +- Duplicate rewards are ignored and required items remain protected from
[stderr] +  destructive progression states or dead ends.
[stderr] +- No authored values, UI, asset, audio, or economy feature is introduced; GATE-
[stderr] +  0004 remains explicit for concrete content implementation.
