[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define deterministic encounter, legal-action, defeat, and one-time reward
[stderr] +resolution contracts for the first battle. It establishes shared rules and
[stderr] +envelopes without party/enemy shapes, balance values, or presentation.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0003 supplies deterministic fixtures and R0004 supplies immutable command,
[stderr] +event, invariant, and RNG contracts. Neither ownership transfers here.
[stderr] +GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete party, enemy, and
[stderr] +balance shapes; it does not defer this contract's authoring.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/core/campaign/{encounter,reward}*` and
[stderr] +  `tests/core/campaign/encounter*`.
[stderr] +- Encounter/action/defeat and reward envelopes, including stable reward IDs.
[stderr] +- Shared encounter commands and deterministic resolution/rejection rules.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define encounter lifecycle states and legal actions as data-driven contracts
[stderr] +that use the core deterministic RNG state. Validate encounter status, expected
[stderr] +revision, action eligibility, targets, and interaction identity before any
[stderr] +resolution. Illegal, stale, or unavailable actions reject without mutation.
[stderr] +Defeat produces a safe typed outcome without silently granting success or
[stderr] +destroying required progress. A reward can be applied only by an eligible
[stderr] +resolved outcome and its stable reward ID grants once; retries return the
[stderr] +recorded result without duplicate reward application.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Web and PWA adapters send the same action commands and render returned events.
[stderr] +Animation timing, combat controls, haptics, sound, renderer choices, offline
[stderr] +shell lifecycle, and browser storage are outside the shared contract.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not introduce multiplayer, live balance, concrete combatants, authored
[stderr] +stats, visual effects, combat art, audio, UI, mid-combat save guarantees,
[stderr] +network services, or presentation state. Do not resolve GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: encounter and reward envelopes contain no
[stderr] +art/source asset. Do not create or reserve character, enemy, effect, icon,
[stderr] +sprite, texture, map, font, or other visual product asset; `asset_ids` remains
[stderr] +blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: deterministic resolution does not own music
[stderr] +or sound-effect selection, triggers, or playback. Keep audio IDs and other
[stderr] +audio metadata blank/default and create no incidental cues.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Run deterministic fixture pairs with the same RNG state and assert identical
[stderr] +  legal action results, events, defeat outcomes, and reward application.
[stderr] +- Prove illegal actions, stale revisions, unavailable targets, and duplicate
[stderr] +  interaction/reward IDs preserve state or return the recorded prior outcome.
[stderr] +- Compare metadata, requirements, ownership, provenance, and dependencies with
[stderr] +  IMP-0015 and R0015's manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain deterministic encounter fixture output, invalid-action and duplicate-
[stderr] +reward results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and the retained GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Only legal encounter actions resolve; invalid actions do not mutate state.
[stderr] +- Defeat is safe and reward IDs apply exactly once under retry/replay.
[stderr] +- Concrete combatants, balance, art, audio, and UI remain out of scope, while
[stderr] +  GATE-0004 remains explicit for later implementation.
