[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define the shared, content-neutral scene, exit, collision, and interaction
[stderr] +transition contract that preserves a completable route. This task owns rules
[stderr] +and envelopes only, not maps, presentation, or authored campaign content.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0004 provides immutable state, commands, events, and invariants; R0005
[stderr] +provides the content schema and reference validator. Both remain their owners.
[stderr] +GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete scene, locale, map, and
[stderr] +content shapes; it does not defer this contract's authoring.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/core/campaign/scene*` and `tests/core/campaign/scene*`.
[stderr] +- The scene and exit envelope, including stable scene/exit/interaction IDs.
[stderr] +- Shared scene-transition commands and route-graph validation boundary.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Model scene entry, available exits, collision/interaction eligibility, and
[stderr] +transition outcomes as deterministic shared-core data. Validate references,
[stderr] +the expected revision, current-scene membership, predicate eligibility, and
[stderr] +destination reachability before mutating state. An invalid, blocked, stale, or
[stderr] +unknown exit returns a typed rejection and leaves state unchanged. A validated
[stderr] +route graph must identify a start-to-completion path without adding concrete
[stderr] +map geometry or authored locations.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Responsive web and installed PWA adapters submit the same scene commands and
[stderr] +render returned state/events. They may translate input or visual collision
[stderr] +signals into commands but cannot interpret or mutate campaign transitions.
[stderr] +Rendering, navigation layout, browser history, cache lifecycle, and PWA
[stderr] +installation are outside this shared-core contract.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not create UI, maps, extra regions, procedural worlds, authored locations,
[stderr] +dialogue, assets, audio, input handling, browser navigation, persistence
[stderr] +drivers, or concrete content values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: scene envelopes and validation do not need
[stderr] +visual or source assets. Do not create or reserve incidental maps, tiles,
[stderr] +sprites, icons, textures, illustrations, fonts, or other product assets;
[stderr] +`asset_ids` remains blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract neither selects nor triggers
[stderr] +music or sound effects. Keep audio IDs, brief, and style version blank; do not
[stderr] +create incidental cues.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Use deterministic fixtures to show invalid exits, unknown references, stale
[stderr] +  commands, and blocked predicates leave the exact prior state unchanged.
[stderr] +- Validate a minimal abstract route graph and reject an unreachable destination
[stderr] +  or invalid exit reference without introducing authored maps or locations.
[stderr] +- Compare metadata, ownership, requirements, provenance, and dependencies with
[stderr] +  IMP-0013 and the R0013 manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain fixture output for rejected and legal transitions, route-graph validator
[stderr] +results, the ownership comparison, and the recorded unresolved GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Scene, exit, collision, and interaction transitions are shared-core,
[stderr] +  deterministic, reference-checked, and content-neutral.
[stderr] +- Invalid exits and references do not mutate state, and route validation proves
[stderr] +  a completable abstract path.
[stderr] +- GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content implementation; no UI,
[stderr] +  authored map, visual asset, or audio work is introduced.
