/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:21:(`IMP-0001` through `IMP-0012`) is allocated exactly once. The dispatcher\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-22-therefore created [`D0002`](../authoring-runbooks/D0002.md) as the sole\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-23-successor, without advancing B/R counters or modifying accepted work.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-24-\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-32-| 4 | B0004 | R0005, R0006 | After B0003; R0006 waits for GATE-0003 | Validate content/save separation |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-33-| 5 | B0005 | R0007, R0009, R0011 | After B0004; R0007/GATE-0003 and R0009/GATE-0005 remain blocked | Validate migration, diagnostics, provenance |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-34-| 6 | B0006 | R0012 | After B0003 and B0004; safe in parallel with B0005 after B0004 | Cross-check foundation documentation and gates |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:35:| 7 | B0007 | R0013, R0014, R0015, R0016 | After B0003; GATE-0004 retained | Validate domain-state seams and non-asset boundaries |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:36:| 8 | B0008 | R0017, R0018, R0019, R0020 | After B0007; GATE-0004/provenance retained | Validate campaign integration, asset reservation, and SHARD-03 handoff |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-37-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-38-The batches are deliberately smaller than seven where a contract is context-heavy (state, persistence, content) or tightly coupled to its predecessor. Together they form an incremental foundation vertical slice: reproducible baseline, shared seams/test harness, deterministic game state and P0 exclusion, content and recovery bounda