ded:\n\n```yaml\nasset_impact: required # or not_applicable\nasset_ids: village_gate_main,village_gate_construction # blank only when not_applicable\n```\n\nFor `asset_impact: required`, the B-series writer must reserve stable,\nproduct-specific asset IDs (never generic names such as `image1`), provide an\n`asset_brief` and `visual_style_version`, and include an `## Asset assessment`\nsection explaining the assets' purpose, where they appear, the required visual\nstates/variants, source-of-truth ownership, and original-art acceptance checks.\nFor `not_applicable`, that section must explain why the scope needs no generated\nor source visual asset and explicitly prohibit incidental asset creation. This\nkeeps UI, illustration, icon, texture, sprite, audio-visual, and other product\nasset work visible in the implementation plan instead of discovering it midway\nthrough coding.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must also declare an audio assessment, even\nwhen audio is not needed:\n\n```yaml\naudio_impact: required # or not_applicable\naudio_ids: ember_menu_loop # blank only when not_applicable\naudio_brief: 30-second seamless instrumental menu cue # blank only when not_applicable\naudio_duration_seconds: 30 # 0 only when not_applicable\naudio_loop: required # required, not_required, or not_applicable\naudio_style_version: project-audio-v1\n```\n\nFor `audio_impact: required`, the writer must reserve stable cue IDs, cite the\nrelevant `04-audio-direction.md` section, describe the in-product trigger and\nmix/accessibility expectations, and assign a sensible duration and loop policy.\nThe Supervisor's separate local audio lane then creates a manifest, invokes\nACE-Step, and performs technical/provenance QA before coding begins. For\n`not_applicable`, every audio field has the stated empty/default form so an\notherwise unrelated task cannot silently generate music or sound effects.\n\nFor any contract allocated from an asset family or audio cue map, `required` is\nmandatory\u2014not a stylistic choice. The writer must not mark a game content,\npresentation, asset-pipeline, music, sound-effect, or cue-integration contract\nas `not_applicable` merely because a prior foundation wave has not created the\nasset yet. It must cite the relevant canonical asset/audio direction and own\nthe stable IDs needed by the separate implementation supervisor.\n\nEach B-series authoring task may create at most seven R-series implementation\nrunbooks. It must stop after its assigned seven (or fewer), update the manifest,\nrecords, and only these specification sections: `03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,\n`03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency`,\n`04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour`, and\n`04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy`.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `../runbooks/R0002.md` \u2014 IMP-0002; dependencies R0001.\n- `../runbooks/R0003.md` \u2014 IMP-0003; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n- `../runbooks/R0010.md` \u2014 IMP-0010; dependencies R0001,R0002.\n\n## Required authoring content\n\nFor each output, use standard Supervisor front matter and the exact manifest\nprovenance (`source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch:\nB0002`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`) plus `asset_impact:\nnot_applicable` and blank `asset_ids`, plus `audio_impact: not_applicable`,\nblank `audio_ids`, `audio_brief`, and `audio_style_version`,\n`audio_duration_seconds: 0`, and `audio_loop: not_applicable`. Make each an individually implementable\ntask containing objective, dependencies, relevant requirements, ownership,\nbehaviour, non-goals, web/PWA differences, verification/evidence, observable\nacceptance criteria, and an `## Asset assessment` that prohibits incidental\nassets.\n\n## Validation procedure\n\nRefuse a conflicting existing R ID or path. Load every output, compare all\nmetadata and dependencies to the manifest, verify provenance fields are\nnon-empty, and verify that all three outputs have the required sections.\n\n## Checkpoint and update procedure\n\nUpdate only B0002's checkpoint/state after all three outputs validate. Preserve\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0002.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md; sed -n '1,180p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n---\ntask_id: R0012\nsequence: 12\ntitle: Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\ndependencies: R0002,R0004,R0006,R0008\nrequirement_ids: NFR-0012,NFR-0010,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability,specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics,specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0012\nauthoring_batch: B0006\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nCreate the bounded developer-documentation closure for the SHARD-01 foundation.\nIt cross-references the approved planning contracts for architecture ownership,\ncommand flow, save-versus-cache recovery, and P0 connected-scope exclusion.\nIt is documentation work only: it neither implements these boundaries nor\nclaims their approval, product completion, or release readiness.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0002 defines the shared-core and adapter seam; R0004 owns deterministic\ncampaign-state transitions; R0006 owns the local save and recovery protocol;\nand R0008 owns the P0 identity and connected-service exclusion. Their listed\ncontracts are prerequisites for this index, not evidence that implementation\nor the B0004 checkpoint has been accepted. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 for\nstorage, quota, support, and recovery-policy choices, and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006\nfor any connected scope. No documented gate is resolved here.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `docs/architecture.md` foundation component, dependency-direction, and\n  public-boundary inventory.\n- `docs/development.md` command-flow, validation, and ownership cross-reference.\n- `docs/save-and-recovery.md` save-versus-preference-versus-cache boundary and\n  recovery index.\n- `docs/security-boundary.md` P0 local-profile and connected-scope exclusion.\n- Foundation decision and ownership index, and the documented public-boundary\n  inventory.\n\nThis contract owns the required documentation set and its cross-reference\nindex only. R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008 retain ownership of their seams,\nstate, persistence protocol, negative boundary tests, and any implementation\noutputs. Content validation, migration execution, PWA release/cache lifecycle,\ndiagnostics, assets, and audio remain with their respective current or future\ncontracts.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nDocument the foundation architecture as a shared deterministic rules core,\ncontent validator, browser presentation/input adapters, local save/recovery\nrepository, PWA release manager, and error/diagnostic boundary. State the\ndirection of interaction: adapters issue commands, only the rules core produces\ndurable campaign state, and the shell renders returned state/events without\nmutating campaign state. Browser APIs, timers, network calls, and renderer\ndependencies remain outside the core.\n\nDocument that the save repository owns serialized snapshots and recovery\nmetadata, while the shell owns ephemeral UI state. Record the write-ahead\nreplacement boundary: validate a complete candidate and read-back before\npromoting a current pointer, retain a known-good snapshot, and quarantine\ninvalid or incompatible candidates. Preferences and PWA cache records are not\nsaves and cannot promote, overwrite, delete, synchronise, or imply success for\na campaign snapshot. Migration transformations remain a later pure-runner\nconcern; this index must not choose storage, quota, retention, support window,\nor migration policy.\n\nDocument P0 as an offline local-profile boundary with no account, token, role,\nremote profile, network client, cloud save, analytics transport, entitlement,\nor connected campaign authority. Treat persisted bytes, content, browser\nevents, URL parameters, and service-worker messages as untrusted at their\nrespective boundaries. Any future connected proposal remains separately gated\nand cannot redefine the local campaign as non-authoritative.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nResponsive web and installed PWA share the same core, command, local-save,\npreference, quarantine, and connected-scope boundaries. The PWA release/cache\nmanager may manage install and cached-release lifecycle but must remain separate\nfrom campaign persistence: a cache refresh, update, or offline failure cannot\nalter a confirmed save. This documentation does not select a browser-storage\nmechanism, service-worker rollout policy, browser matrix, or PWA implementation.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not implement or approve a framework, renderer, storage API, quota,\nretention or support policy, migration set, diagnostics vendor or transport,\nidentity, authorization, remote service, cloud sync, telemetry, purchase,\nentitlement, rollout, release operation, or player-facing release guide. Do\nnot claim vendor, security, privacy, legal, product, or release approval. Do\nnot create gameplay, UI, content, assets, audio, source implementation, or\ntest fixtures beyond the documentation contract described above.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: foundation documentation and its ownership\nindex need no product asset. Do not create or reserve incidental visual, source,\naudio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other product asset;\n`asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Load this runbook and compare its task ID, sequence, title, catalogue ID,\n  requirement IDs, source specifications, dependencies, authoring batch,\n  factory stages, and asset/audio/browser decisions with the R0012 manifest\n  allocation and IMP-0012 catalogue record.\n- Cross-check the documentation index against R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008:\n  each prerequisite's ownership, dependency boundary, and retained gate must\n  be named without transferring ownership or claiming implementation status.\n- Confirm the index distinguishes durable campaign state, serialized snapshot\n  and recovery metadata, preferences, PWA cache, shell UI state, and future\n  connected scope; confirm it contains no storage/vendor/policy selection.\n- Confirm the documentation records GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 /\n  DEC-0006 as unresolved. If R0006 or B0004 is blocked, preserve that state in\n  the cross-check; do not mark the foundation, a gate, or a release accepted.\n- Record the B0006 checkpoint only after every comparison succeeds. On a\n  mismatch or existing conflicting R0012 contract, stop, retain the allocated\n  ID and path, and repair or report only this documentation contract; never\n  overwrite, reuse, renumber, or replace an R ID.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain the loader result; manifest and IMP-0012 comparison record; the\nfoundation ownership/dependency/gate matrix for R0002, R0004, R0006, and R0008;\nthe save/preference/cache and local/connected-boundary review; all retained\nGATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 records; and the successful\npre-checkpoint validation record. These are contract-review artefacts, not\nevidence of implementation, approval, or release readiness.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The developer-documentation closure maps every listed foundation prerequisite\n  to its retained ownership, dependency boundary, and unresolved gate without\n  transferring implementation ownership or claiming acceptance.\n- Architecture, command flow, save/recovery, preference/cache separation, and\n  P0 connected-scope exclusion remain explicit for both responsive web and PWA\n  delivery paths.\n- No product asset, implementation, approval, vendor/policy choice, or release\n  readiness claim is introduced; GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and GATE-0006 / DEC-0006\n  remain visible.\n---\ntask_id: R0004\nsequence: 4\ntitle: Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\ndependencies: R0002,R0003\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0010\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract,specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0004\nauthoring_batch: B0003\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; state envelopes deliberately exclude authored content.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine the immutable, versioned shared campaign-state, command, result, event,\nrevision, interaction-ID, and deterministic-RNG contracts needed to validate\nlegal transitions. This foundation defines envelopes and invariants only; it\ndoes not introduce a feature state machine or authored campaign values.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0002 provides the shared-core/adapter seam and R0003 provides deterministic\nfixtures. They are implementation dependencies, not authoring blockers.\nRetain GATE-0004: concrete party and content shapes remain unapproved.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/`.\n- The versioned campaign-snapshot envelope and deterministic RNG state.\n- The public core command, state, event, result, revision, and interaction-ID\n  interfaces, plus `tests/core/contract.*`.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nMake state transitions pure and explicit: a command carries an expected\ncampaign revision and stable interaction/action ID; processing returns either\na typed rejection with no mutation or ordered state/events with a new revision.\nValidate command shape, session state, identifiers, availability, eligibility,\npredicates, and expected revision before any transition. Invariant helpers\nmust reject invalid state and preserve the prior immutable state.\n\nRecord deterministic RNG seed/state at safe boundaries. Require idempotency for\nretries: a duplicate interaction ID or acknowledged durable transition returns\nits prior result without a second reward, checkpoint, or revision-changing\ntransition. Process one command at a time per active campaign and reject stale\nwriters so visibility changes, repeated input, and concurrent tabs cannot\ninterleave a transition.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nWeb and PWA adapters submit the same shared command envelopes and consume the\nsame state/event results. Platform adapters may debounce controls and manage a\nlocal slot lease/read-only warning, but neither gains authority to mutate state\ndirectly. Installation, cache lifecycle, and storage-driver work are outside\nthis contract.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not author content values; implement combat, inventory, quest, exploration,\nor UI state machines; select party shapes; implement a save driver or cache;\nadd account, identity, token, role, network, or remote state; or create assets,\naudio, maps, dialogue, or reference-derived content.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: these serializable state and interface\ncontracts deliberately exclude authored content. Do not create or reserve\nincidental visual, source, audio, font, icon, illustration, texture, sprite,\nmap, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Use R0003 deterministic fixtures to prove invalid commands leave the exact\n  prior state unchanged and stale revisions reject without mutation.\n- Prove a duplicate interaction ID returns the recorded prior outcome and\n  produces no additional durable transition.\n- Exercise controlled RNG state twice and compare state/event results.\n- Exercise sequential command handling and a stale-writer fixture without\n  selecting a browser-storage implementation.\n- Record GATE-0004 as retained before adding concrete party/content shapes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain contract-test output for invalid, stale, duplicate, deterministic-RNG,\nand serialized transition cases, plus the public envelope/invariant inventory\nand the retained GATE-0004 record.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Invalid or stale commands cannot mutate campaign state.\n- Duplicate interaction IDs are idempotent and cause no extra durable\n  transition.\n- State, command, result, event, revision, and RNG contracts are shared-core\n  only, versioned where serialized, and independent of concrete content,\n  persistence drivers, or connected scope.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The four manifest allocations are present and their target paths are absent. I\u2019m now authoring the bounded contracts with exact provenance, dependencies, and retained GATE-0004 language.\",\"changed_files\":[],\"test_result\":\"\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Verified B0007 and manifest ownership before writing.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"runbooks/F014.md\",\"runbooks/TEMPLATE.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0007.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\"],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"No general README update is needed: this task creates the assigned implementation runbook contracts only.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"Domain-only shared-core contract authoring; no browser behavior or Playwright spec applies.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0013.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0014.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0015.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0013.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0013.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..51d04ce078dd3b4365d6a5dd29b03a3872bb33e2\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0013.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0013\n+sequence: 13\n+title: Define exploration scene and exit transition contract\n+dependencies: R0004,R0005\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0013\n+authoring_batch: B0007\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; content-neutral scene and transition contracts.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the shared, content-neutral scene, exit, collision, and interaction\n+transition contract that preserves a completable route. This task owns rules\n+and envelopes only, not maps, presentation, or authored campaign content.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0004 provides immutable state, commands, events, and invariants; R0005\n+provides the content schema and reference validator. Both remain their owners.\n+GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete scene, locale, map, and\n+content shapes; it does not defer this contract's authoring.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/scene*` and `tests/core/campaign/scene*`.\n+- The scene and exit envelope, including stable scene/exit/interaction IDs.\n+- Shared scene-transition commands and route-graph validation boundary.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Model scene entry, available exits, collision/interaction eligibility, and\n+transition outcomes as deterministic shared-core data. Validate references,\n+the expected revision, current-scene membership, predicate eligibility, and\n+destination reachability before mutating state. An invalid, blocked, stale, or\n+unknown exit returns a typed rejection and leaves state unchanged. A validated\n+route graph must identify a start-to-completion path without adding concrete\n+map geometry or authored locations.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA adapters submit the same scene commands and\n+render returned state/events. They may translate input or visual collision\n+signals into commands but cannot interpret or mutate campaign transitions.\n+Rendering, navigation layout, browser history, cache lifecycle, and PWA\n+installation are outside this shared-core contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create UI, maps, extra regions, procedural worlds, authored locations,\n+dialogue, assets, audio, input handling, browser navigation, persistence\n+drivers, or concrete content values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: scene envelopes and validation do not need\n+visual or source assets. Do not create or reserve incidental maps, tiles,\n+sprites, icons, textures, illustrations, fonts, or other product assets;\n+`asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract neither selects nor triggers\n+music or sound effects. Keep audio IDs, brief, and style version blank; do not\n+create incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic fixtures to show invalid exits, unknown references, stale\n+  commands, and blocked predicates leave the exact prior state unchanged.\n+- Validate a minimal abstract route graph and reject an unreachable destination\n+  or invalid exit reference without introducing authored maps or locations.\n+- Compare metadata, ownership, requirements, provenance, and dependencies with\n+  IMP-0013 and the R0013 manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain fixture output for rejected and legal transitions, route-graph validator\n+results, the ownership comparison, and the recorded unresolved GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Scene, exit, collision, and interaction transitions are shared-core,\n+  deterministic, reference-checked, and content-neutral.\n+- Invalid exits and references do not mutate state, and route validation proves\n+  a completable abstract path.\n+- GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content implementation; no UI,\n+  authored map, visual asset, or audio work is introduced.\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0014.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0014.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..859f7a992ec271de91548e8459b8e085add0e43b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0014.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0014\n+sequence: 14\n+title: Define narrative quest and tutorial state transitions\n+dependencies: R0004,R0013\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0005,REQ-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending,specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0014\n+authoring_batch: B0007\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No authored dialogue or assets; state/predicate contracts only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define original-content-neutral dialogue, quest, tutorial, and campaign-state\n+rules that make required progression explicit and idempotent. This contract\n+defines progression mechanics, not story text, presentation, or authored\n+campaign expression.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0004 owns the core command/idempotency contract and R0013 owns scene and\n+interaction transitions. Their outputs are prerequisites, not transferred\n+ownership. GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for authored text, locale,\n+and content detail; it does not defer this contract's authoring.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/{quest,dialogue,tutorial}*` and\n+  `tests/core/campaign/quest*`.\n+- Quest, dialogue, tutorial, predicate, and progression envelopes.\n+- Shared progression commands and idempotent completion/rejection rules.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Represent progression as stable identifiers, explicit states, prerequisites,\n+and predicates. Validate interaction IDs, expected revisions, state\n+preconditions, and predicate inputs before completing tutorial or quest steps.\n+Completion is idempotent: repeating an acknowledged interaction returns its\n+prior outcome and never repeats a transition, reward, or required-state loss.\n+Invalid predicates and missing prerequisites reject safely without mutation.\n+Required campaign progression cannot be bypassed, overwritten, or made\n+unreachable by optional state.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and PWA adapters render and submit the same shared progression commands.\n+They may provide presentation-specific onboarding affordances but have no\n+authority to mark dialogue, tutorial, or quest progress complete. UI flow,\n+layout, localization rendering, and PWA lifecycle are excluded.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not author story, dialogue, locale strings, characters, branches, user\n+content, UI, assets, audio, maps, rewards, browser flows, or remote state. Do\n+not resolve GATE-0004 or select concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: predicate and progression contracts need\n+no visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve dialogue portraits, maps,\n+icons, illustrations, fonts, sprites, or any other product asset; `asset_ids`\n+remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: state transitions neither select nor\n+trigger music, speech, or sound effects. Keep all audio metadata blank/default\n+and do not create incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Exercise repeated completion through deterministic fixtures and prove it\n+  returns the acknowledged outcome without an extra transition or reward.\n+- Prove invalid predicates, missing prerequisites, stale revisions, and unknown\n+  identifiers reject without state mutation or bypassing required progress.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to\n+  IMP-0014 and R0014's manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain progression state-machine fixture output, idempotency/rejection results,\n+the manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved GATE-0004 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Quest and tutorial progression is explicit, predicate-checked, repeat-safe,\n+  and cannot bypass required campaign state.\n+- Repeated completion is idempotent and invalid progression commands preserve\n+  the prior state.\n+- No authored narrative, locale, UI, asset, or audio work is introduced, and\n+  GATE-0004 remains visible as an implementation gate.\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0015.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0015.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3b6308ab32d57145a1a6759f0ae48f56c66e4596\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0015.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,99 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0015\n+sequence: 15\n+title: Define deterministic encounter and reward resolution contract\n+dependencies: R0003,R0004\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0003,REQ-0005,NFR-0002\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#4-party-combat-encounters-rewards-and-balance,specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0015\n+authoring_batch: B0007\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No combat art, audio, enemies, or balance values.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define deterministic encounter, legal-action, defeat, and one-time reward\n+resolution contracts for the first battle. It establishes shared rules and\n+envelopes without party/enemy shapes, balance values, or presentation.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0003 supplies deterministic fixtures and R0004 supplies immutable command,\n+event, invariant, and RNG contracts. Neither ownership transfers here.\n+GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete party, enemy, and\n+balance shapes; it does not defer this contract's authoring.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/{encounter,reward}*` and\n+  `tests/core/campaign/encounter*`.\n+- Encounter/action/defeat and reward envelopes, including stable reward IDs.\n+- Shared encounter commands and deterministic resolution/rejection rules.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Define encounter lifecycle states and legal actions as data-driven contracts\n+that use the core deterministic RNG state. Validate encounter status, expected\n+revision, action eligibility, targets, and interaction identity before any\n+resolution. Illegal, stale, or unavailable actions reject without mutation.\n+Defeat produces a safe typed outcome without silently granting success or\n+destroying required progress. A reward can be applied only by an eligible\n+resolved outcome and its stable reward ID grants once; retries return the\n+recorded result without duplicate reward application.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and PWA adapters send the same action commands and render returned events.\n+Animation timing, combat controls, haptics, sound, renderer choices, offline\n+shell lifecycle, and browser storage are outside the shared contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not introduce multiplayer, live balance, concrete combatants, authored\n+stats, visual effects, combat art, audio, UI, mid-combat save guarantees,\n+network services, or presentation state. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: encounter and reward envelopes contain no\n+art/source asset. Do not create or reserve character, enemy, effect, icon,\n+sprite, texture, map, font, or other visual product asset; `asset_ids` remains\n+blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: deterministic resolution does not own music\n+or sound-effect selection, triggers, or playback. Keep audio IDs and other\n+audio metadata blank/default and create no incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run deterministic fixture pairs with the same RNG state and assert identical\n+  legal action results, events, defeat outcomes, and reward application.\n+- Prove illegal actions, stale revisions, unavailable targets, and duplicate\n+  interaction/reward IDs preserve state or return the recorded prior outcome.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, ownership, provenance, and dependencies with\n+  IMP-0015 and R0015's manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain deterministic encounter fixture output, invalid-action and duplicate-\n+reward results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and the retained GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Only legal encounter actions resolve; invalid actions do not mutate state.\n+- Defeat is safe and reward IDs apply exactly once under retry/replay.\n+- Concrete combatants, balance, art, audio, and UI remain out of scope, while\n+  GATE-0004 remains explicit for later implementation.\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..346c0ba2d1def091dcef92d9fbc75da873c2e3fb\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0016\n+sequence: 16\n+title: Define safe inventory and party progression contract\n+dependencies: R0004,R0015\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0004,REQ-0008,NFR-0002\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#5-inventory-party-progression-and-economy,specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0016\n+authoring_batch: B0007\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No item art or authored values; rules only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define eligibility-checked inventory, party progression, and stable reward\n+application rules that protect required items and prevent dead ends. This task\n+owns shared contracts, not authored items, values, presentation, or economy.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0004 provides immutable state and idempotent commands; R0015 provides stable\n+reward resolution and one-time reward IDs. Their implementation ownership\n+remains intact. GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for authored item and\n+progression shapes; it does not defer this contract's authoring.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/{inventory,party}*` and\n+  `tests/core/campaign/inventory*`.\n+- Item, eligibility, party-progression, and reward-application envelopes.\n+- Shared inventory commands and protected-required-item invariants.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Model inventory and party progression using stable identifiers, explicit\n+eligibility predicates, and immutable transitions. Validate item existence,\n+ownership, expected revision, target eligibility, prerequisite state, and the\n+originating reward before mutation. Ineligible use, missing items, duplicate\n+reward application, and stale commands are no-ops with typed rejection or the\n+recorded prior outcome. Required items cannot be destructively discarded,\n+consumed, traded, or overwritten in a way that makes the required abstract\n+route impossible.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and PWA adapters submit the same inventory/progression commands and render\n+the returned state/events. Inventory controls, drag/drop, responsive layout,\n+notifications, persistence-driver choices, and installed-PWA lifecycle are\n+outside this contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not author items, party members, progression values, inventory UI, crafting,\n+trading, purchases, destructive discard, art, audio, maps, remote state, or\n+browser/PWA behavior. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: abstract inventory and party rules need no\n+visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve item icons, portraits, sprites,\n+textures, fonts, illustrations, maps, or other product assets; `asset_ids`\n+remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract owns no music or sound-effect\n+trigger, selection, or mix. Keep audio IDs, brief, and style version blank and\n+do not create incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic fixtures to prove eligibility is checked before mutation\n+  and that missing/ineligible/stale commands preserve the exact prior state.\n+- Prove duplicate reward IDs do not apply twice and protected required items\n+  cannot be lost in a way that removes the required abstract route.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, dependencies, ownership, and provenance with\n+  IMP-0016 and R0016's manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain inventory/progression rejection fixtures, duplicate-reward and\n+protected-item invariant results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and the\n+unresolved GATE-0004 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Eligibility is validated before inventory or party-progression mutation.\n+- Duplicate rewards are ignored and required items remain protected from\n+  destructive progression states or dead ends.\n+- No authored values, UI, asset, audio, or economy feature is introduced; GATE-\n+  0004 remains explicit for concrete content implementation.\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0013.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0013.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..51d04ce078dd3b4365d6a5dd29b03a3872bb33e2\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0013.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0013\n+sequence: 13\n+title: Define exploration scene and exit transition contract\n+dependencies: R0004,R0005\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0013\n+authoring_batch: B0007\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; content-neutral scene and transition contracts.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the shared, content-neutral scene, exit, collision, and interaction\n+transition contract that preserves a completable route. This task owns rules\n+and envelopes only, not maps, presentation, or authored campaign content.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0004 provides immutable state, commands, events, and invariants; R0005\n+provides the content schema and reference validator. Both remain their owners.\n+GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete scene, locale, map, and\n+content shapes; it does not defer this contract's authoring.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/scene*` and `tests/core/campaign/scene*`.\n+- The scene and exit envelope, including stable scene/exit/interaction IDs.\n+- Shared scene-transition commands and route-graph validation boundary.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Model scene entry, available exits, collision/interaction eligibility, and\n+transition outcomes as deterministic shared-core data. Validate references,\n+the expected revision, current-scene membership, predicate eligibility, and\n+destination reachability before mutating state. An invalid, blocked, stale, or\n+unknown exit returns a typed rejection and leaves state unchanged. A validated\n+route graph must identify a start-to-completion path without adding concrete\n+map geometry or authored locations.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA adapters submit the same scene commands and\n+render returned state/events. They may translate input or visual collision\n+signals into commands but cannot interpret or mutate campaign transitions.\n+Rendering, navigation layout, browser history, cache lifecycle, and PWA\n+installation are outside this shared-core contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create UI, maps, extra regions, procedural worlds, authored locations,\n+dialogue, assets, audio, input handling, browser navigation, persistence\n+drivers, or concrete content values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: scene envelopes and validation do not need\n+visual or source assets. Do not create or reserve incidental maps, tiles,\n+sprites, icons, textures, illustrations, fonts, or other product assets;\n+`asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract neither selects nor triggers\n+music or sound effects. Keep audio IDs, brief, and style version blank; do not\n+create incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic fixtures to show invalid exits, unknown references, stale\n+  commands, and blocked predicates leave the exact prior state unchanged.\n+- Validate a minimal abstract route graph and reject an unreachable destination\n+  or invalid exit reference without introducing authored maps or locations.\n+- Compare metadata, ownership, requirements, provenance, and dependencies with\n+  IMP-0013 and the R0013 manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain fixture output for rejected and legal transitions, route-graph validator\n+results, the ownership comparison, and the recorded unresolved GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Scene, exit, collision, and interaction transitions are shared-core,\n+  deterministic, reference-checked, and content-neutral.\n+- Invalid exits and references do not mutate state, and route validation proves\n+  a completable abstract path.\n+- GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content implementation; no UI,\n+  authored map, visual asset, or audio work is introduced.\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0014.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0014.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..859f7a992ec271de91548e8459b8e085add0e43b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0014.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0014\n+sequence: 14\n+title: Define narrative quest and tutorial state transitions\n+dependencies: R0004,R0013\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0005,REQ-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending,specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0014\n+authoring_batch: B0007\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No authored dialogue or assets; state/predicate contracts only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define original-content-neutral dialogue, quest, tutorial, and campaign-state\n+rules that make required progression explicit and idempotent. This contract\n+defines progression mechanics, not story text, presentation, or authored\n+campaign expression.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0004 owns the core command/idempotency contract and R0013 owns scene and\n+interaction transitions. Their outputs are prerequisites, not transferred\n+ownership. GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for authored text, locale,\n+and content detail; it does not defer this contract's authoring.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/{quest,dialogue,tutorial}*` and\n+  `tests/core/campaign/quest*`.\n+- Quest, dialogue, tutorial, predicate, and progression envelopes.\n+- Shared progression commands and idempotent completion/rejection rules.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Represent progression as stable identifiers, explicit states, prerequisites,\n+and predicates. Validate interaction IDs, expected revisions, state\n+preconditions, and predicate inputs before completing tutorial or quest steps.\n+Completion is idempotent: repeating an acknowledged interaction returns its\n+prior outcome and never repeats a transition, reward, or required-state loss.\n+Invalid predicates and missing prerequisites reject safely without mutation.\n+Required campaign progression cannot be bypassed, overwritten, or made\n+unreachable by optional state.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and PWA adapters render and submit the same shared progression commands.\n+They may provide presentation-specific onboarding affordances but have no\n+authority to mark dialogue, tutorial, or quest progress complete. UI flow,\n+layout, localization rendering, and PWA lifecycle are excluded.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not author story, dialogue, locale strings, characters, branches, user\n+content, UI, assets, audio, maps, rewards, browser flows, or remote state. Do\n+not resolve GATE-0004 or select concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: predicate and progression contracts need\n+no visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve dialogue portraits, maps,\n+icons, illustrations, fonts, sprites, or any other product asset; `asset_ids`\n+remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: state transitions neither select nor\n+trigger music, speech, or sound effects. Keep all audio metadata blank/default\n+and do not create incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Exercise repeated completion through deterministic fixtures and prove it\n+  returns the acknowledged outcome without an extra transition or reward.\n+- Prove invalid predicates, missing prerequisites, stale revisions, and unknown\n+  identifiers reject without state mutation or bypassing required progress.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to\n+  IMP-0014 and R0014's manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain progression state-machine fixture output, idempotency/rejection results,\n+the manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved GATE-0004 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Quest and tutorial progression is explicit, predicate-checked, repeat-safe,\n+  and cannot bypass required campaign state.\n+- Repeated completion is idempotent and invalid progression commands preserve\n+  the prior state.\n+- No authored narrative, locale, UI, asset, or audio work is introduced, and\n+  GATE-0004 remains visible as an implementation gate.\ndiff --git a/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0015.md b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0015.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3b6308ab32d57145a1a6759f0ae48f56c66e4596\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0015.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,99 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0015\n+sequence: 15\n+title: Define deterministic encounter and reward resolution contract\n+dependencies: R0003,R0004\